{
  "_doc": [
    "Shared linkify vectors: ONE contract for both import sides.",
    "Server: api/services/journal_two/note_connectors/convert/linkify.py (test_linkify.py reads this file).",
    "Client: Plan B linkPolicy.js linkifyTextNodes (its test reads this file too), so the two cannot drift.",
    "Each vector: `text` placed in `context`; `links` = the links linkify CREATES, in order, as {text, href}.",
    "context: plain = a paragraph text run; inline_code = a run with a code mark (<code>);",
    "code_block = a codeBlock (<pre>); link = a run already inside a link (<a href=\"https://existing.example/\">);",
    "inline_math / block_math = math nodes (data-type inline-math / block-math). Every non-plain context must come out untouched.",
    "Rule (linkify-it 5 defaults, the same instance markdown-it uses): keep a match only when its schema is http:, https: or",
    "mailto: (a bare email counts; href gets mailto:), or its schema is empty and its raw text starts with www. (case-insensitive;",
    "href gets https://). Every other fuzzy domain (NVDA.US, example.com), ftp: and // is dropped.",
    "Then ONE trim, the same on both sides: cut the match at the first character of",
    "U+3000 U+3001 U+3002 U+FF0C U+FF1B U+FF1A U+FF01 U+FF1F U+FF08 U+FF09 U+3010 U+3011 U+300C U+300D U+300E U+300F U+300A U+300B",
    "U+3008 U+3009 U+201C U+201D U+2018 U+2019 U+2026 (CJK/fullwidth punctuation and curly quotes, which linkify-it keeps inside a",
    "path), then strip trailing . , : ; ! ? characters; then keep the result only if linkify-it matches it again as exactly one",
    "kept link spanning the whole trimmed text.",
    "href_vectors (B-14, controller ruling: every stored link has a door or is plain text): resolve_href / resolveHref of `href`",
    "(against `source` when given) must equal `want`; null = the link becomes plain text. Kept schemes: http(s) (// + a host,",
    "no whitespace, no userinfo, port <= 65535, a numeric last label only as a dotted-quad IPv4), mailto: with an @, tel:/sms:",
    "with a number (digits, optional leading +, spaces - . ( )). `door` (client only) = what linkClickOpen.openableLinkHref opens.",
    "refused_link_vectors (B-14 fix round 1): a link with `href` over `text`; resolve_href refuses it, so the import keeps `text`",
    "exactly as plain text and makes NO link anywhere in it (linkify never re-links a refused link's text). Both sides' import passes."
  ],
  "version": 1,
